Oh! Then this is super easy - just do everything directly on your LFS system in Firefox!
Complete Tutorial - All on LFS with Firefox
Step 1: Clean and create tarball
bash

cd ~/Projects/hspm

# Clean up binaries
rm -f hspm test_recipe_parser test_graph test_checksum test_collision test_symlink
rm -rf test-store/ test-build/ test-live/ distfiles/
rm -f scraper-failures.log test.db

# Create tarball
tar -czf hspm-source.tar.gz \
    --exclude="*.o" \
    --exclude="hspm" \
    --exclude="test_*" \
    --exclude="*.db" \
    --exclude="*.log" \
    --exclude="distfiles" \
    --exclude="test-store" \
    --exclude="test-build" \
    --exclude="test-live" \
    src/ builders/ recipes/ tests/ tools/ Makefile blfs-urls.txt *.md

Step 2: Open Firefox
bash

firefox &

Step 3: Create repository on GitHub

In Firefox:

    Go to https://github.com

    Sign in to your account

    Click the + icon (top-right) → New repository

    Fill in:

        Repository name: hspm

        Description: Hybrid Symlink Package Manager for Linux From Scratch

        Public

        Leave everything else unchecked

    Click Create repository

Step 4: Upload the tarball

On the new repository page:

    Click "uploading an existing file"

    Click "choose your files"

    Navigate to /home/Dev/Projects/hspm/

    Select hspm-source.tar.gz

    Wait for upload

    Add commit message: Initial commit: HSPM source code

    Click Commit changes

Step 5: Add README

After commit:

    Click Add file → Create new file

    Filename: README.md

    Paste this (replace YOUR_USERNAME with your actual GitHub username):

markdown

# HSPM - Hybrid Symlink Package Manager for LFS

A specialized package manager for Linux From Scratch.

## Author

[Your Name] - [Your GitHub Username]

## Features

- **Hybrid tracking** - Adopted (pre-installed) vs Managed packages
- **Nix-style store** - `/opt/hspm/store/` → symlinks → `/usr/`
- **Dependency resolution** with cycle detection
- **Multi-builder** - autotools, cmake, meson, make, perl, python, openssl, waf
- **BLFS scraper** - Auto-generates recipes from BLFS book
- **Crash-safe** - Symlink transactions with rollback
- **RPATH validation** with LD_LIBRARY_PATH support
- **17 unit tests** - All passing

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/hspm.git
cd hspm
make
sudo make install
sudo hspm init
sudo hspm adopt all

Usage
bash

# Install a package
sudo hspm install curl

# Adopt all existing system packages
sudo hspm adopt all

# List installed packages
hspm list

# Verify symlink integrity
sudo hspm verify

# Sync latest BLFS recipes
sudo hspm sync

Requirements

    C++17 compiler

    SQLite3

    Python 3.6+

    wget, tar, make

License

MIT
text


